    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Remote-USA/Senior-Manager--Experimentation-Optimization_R20263526": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Experimentation Optimization",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $78,496.00 - $105,974.00 Position Summary The Senior Manager, Experimentation & Optimization leads conversion rate optimization (CRO) and experimentation for National University’s website and Digital experiences. This is a strategic, data-driven role responsible for defining and executing the CRO roadmap, proactively identifying optimization opportunities, and improving website experiences based on prospective student behavior, user insights, performance data, and lifecycle stage. The primary goal is to increase inquiry, application, and enrollment conversion through data-informed testing, continuous optimization, and an improved user experience. Essential Functions: CRO Strategy & Roadmap Own the CRO and experimentation roadmap for NU’s website and Digital experiences  including opportunity identification, intake, prioritization, sequencing and the testing calendar. Define, execute, and continuously optimize data-driven testing and optimization strategies that improve user experience, engagement, conversion, and content relevance across prospect-facing web experiences. Own website experimentation roadmap, related platform strategy, and associated vendor/partner relationships. Establish testing SLAs, QA standards, governance, and deployment practices that prevent conflicts across concurrent tests, campaigns, and releases. Maintain a repository of hypotheses, test results, learnings, optimization opportunities, and best practices that accelerate knowledge sharing and continuous improvement. Experimentation & Proactive A/B Testing Own the complete experimentation lifecycle: opportunity identification, hypothesis development, prioritization, test design, implementation, QA, launch, measurement, readout, and production rollout of winners. Proactively source the testing pipeline from behavioral analytics, session data, UX research, and website funnel diagnostics rather than operating as a request-driven queue. Design and run A/B, multivariate, and multi-page experiments, ensuring appropriate sample sizing, run length, and statistical significance before a result is acted on. Optimize information architecture, content presentation, navigation, page experience, and calls-to-action using customer insight and behavioral data. Translate experimentation outcomes into optimization recommendations that inform future website roadmaps, experience strategy, and investment priorities. Journey Discovery and Experience Optimization Analyze the end-to-end prospective student journey to identify friction, abandonment, and conversion opportunities using behavioral analytics, session replay, UX research, and customer feedback. Champion continuous optimization of program discovery across web properties, including on-site search, filters, navigation, program finders, and recommendation surfaces. Develop targeted website experience strategies using established audience segments, intent signals, engagement patterns, lifecycle stage, and experimentation insights to improve relevance, engagement, and conversion. Develop and optimize personalized website experiences that deliver relevant messaging, content, navigation, and recommendations based on audience needs, behavioral insights, and lifecycle stage. Partner with Marketing, Enrollment, and Digital Analytics to leverage audience segments, first-party customer data, and behavioral insights to support website personalization and optimization initiatives. Identify opportunities to apply AI-assisted optimization, predictive insights, and behavioral decisioning to improve relevance, engagement, and conversion outcomes. Participate and input into Journey Operations that impact Prospect Student experience in partnership with IT, Accounts, Brand and Product teams. Measurement, KPIs & Reporting Cadence Own measurement best practices, quarterly meta-analysis, CRO Playbook, dashboards, and the KPI framework supporting CRO, experimentation, and website personalization efforts. Define, monitor, and communicate KPIs including experimentation velocity, win rate, conversion improvement, inquiry conversion, application progression, website conversion, journey completion, personalization effectiveness, and incremental business impact. Establish and maintain a regular reporting cadence, including weekly program status, monthly CRO performance readouts, and quarterly roadmap and business-impact reviews for senior leadership. Build executive dashboards and communicate test results, KPI trends, roadmap progress, and strategic recommendations to the Chief Marketing Officer and senior stakeholders. Partner with the Digital Analytics team to establish analytical requirements, measurement plans, and dashboard reporting for UX. Measure the maturity of National University’s experimentation program and continuously evolve optimization capabilities through data-driven insight. Innovation & Continuous Improvement Evaluate emerging trends in AI, personalization, experimentation, behavioral science, and digital experience optimization. Identify opportunities to incorporate intelligent personalization, predictive experiences, and innovative optimization capabilities into National University’s prospective student website experiences. Evaluate new technologies, platforms, and optimization capabilities that strengthen website audience engagement, experience effectiveness, and conversion performance. Continuously benchmark industry trends, competitor experiences, customer expectations, and evolving digital behaviors to identify future opportunities for innovation and growth. Other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsi bilities : Individual contributor role that provides leadership through influence and expertise; scope may evolve over time based on organizational needs. Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, Business, Analytics, Statistics, Human-Computer Interaction, or a related field. Master’s degree or M.B.A. preferred. 7 + years of experience in conversion rate optimization and experimentation, website experience management, personalization, digital merchandising, or e-commerce. 2+ years of experience in a strategy, program ownership, or related manager responsibilities. Demonstrated ownership and administration of A/B testing and personalization platforms (Adobe Target, VWO, Optimizely, or equivalent), including governance, implementation oversight, and optimization best practices. Experience designing, implementing, and optimizing personalized digital experiences using audience segmentation, behavioral targeting, geo-targeting, and journey-based experience targeting. Proven experience developing and executing a CRO and experimentation roadmap, including KPI development, prioritization frameworks, and executive reporting. Experience managing vendors, agency partners, and external development resources to deliver experimentation, personalization, and digital optimization initiatives. Demonstrated track record of leveraging experimentation and personalization strategies to drive measurable improvements in conversion, lead generation, engagement, and business outcomes. Experience in higher education, edtech, or another complex, high-consideration, multi-audience environment preferred. Portfolio, case studies, or documented examples demonstrating measurable conversion improvements and successful optimization initiatives across complex digital ecosystems. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Deep expertise in experimentation methodologies, including hypothesis development, test design, statistical analysis, and interpretation of results to support business decisions. Strong experience leading conversion rate optimization (CRO), personalization, and digital experience optimization programs at scale. Expertise with experimentation, personalization, and analytics platforms such as Adobe Target, Optimizely, VWO, Adobe Analytics, GA4, and FullStory. Strong understanding of customer data platforms, audience segmentation, behavioral targeting, and customer journey optimization. Ability to independently analyze, validate, and interpret complex datasets using SQL, dashboards, and analytics tools to identify opportunities and inform strategy. Experience developing experimentation roadmaps, success metrics, governance processes, and executive reporting frameworks. Strong understanding of UX principles, customer journey mapping, and the integration of qualitative and quantitative insights into optimization strategies. Knowledge of accessibility (WCAG), responsive design principles, content strategy, and technical considerations impacting experimentation and personalization. Experience evaluating and applying emerging technologies, including AI-driven personalization, predictive modeling, and automated decisioning. Exceptional communication, storytelling, stakeholder management, and executive presentation skills, with the ability to translate data into actionable business recommendations. Demonstrated ability to influence and build alignment across Marketing, Product, UX, Technology, Analytics, Enrollment, and other cross-functional teams without direct authority. Strategic mindset with the ability to balance long-term vision, customer needs, operational realities, and measurable business outcomes while driving complex initiatives to completion. Location: Remote, USA Travel: up to 10% travel Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Remote-USA/Senior-UX-Strategist_R20263517-1": {
      "title": "Senior UX Strategist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $78,496.00 - $105,974.00 Position Summary The Senior UX Strategist is responsible for shaping and optimizing end-to-end customer experiences across the prospective student journey through research, journey strategy, customer discovery, service design, and innovation. This role leads user research, journey mapping, design thinking, and requirements gathering to uncover customer needs, identify experience opportunities, and translate insights into actionable strategies and scalable solutions. Working cross-functionally with Product, Design, Analytics, Marketing, and Technology teams. The Senior UX Strategist drives alignment, influences decision-making, and helps create customer-centered digital experiences that improve engagement, conversion, and overall user outcomes. Essential Functions: Experience Strategy & Journey Mapping Lead end-to-end prospective student journey mapping, service blueprinting, and experience strategy initiatives across National University's digital ecosystem. Define current-state and future-state prospective student journeys, identifying friction points, unmet needs, moments that matter, and opportunities to improve engagement, inquiry, application progression, and enrollment outcomes. Translate prospective student insights, institutional priorities, and business objectives into experience strategies, journey roadmaps, and prioritized recommendations that influence digital product and UX roadmaps. Develop experience frameworks, journey principles, and future-state vision artifacts that guide customer-centered digital experiences across the prospective student lifecycle. Partner with Marketing, Enrollment, Product, and Digital teams to align prospective student journey priorities with institutional goals and long-term digital strategy. User Research & Discovery Develop and own the UX research strategy and roadmap supporting prospective student experience initiatives. Lead and execute qualitative and quantitative research, including stakeholder interviews, prospective student interviews, usability testing, surveys, concept validation, diary studies, and behavioral research. Synthesize customer insights, behavioral analytics, market research, competitive analysis, and voice-of-the-customer findings into strategic recommendations that shape experience strategy and digital priorities. Establish and mature UX research standards, repositories, tools, governance, and knowledge-sharing practices that strengthen organizational understanding of prospective student behaviors and needs. Manage research vendors, participant recruitment, research operations, budgets, and external partnerships to ensure high-quality research execution. Partner with the Digital Analytics team to combine qualitative and quantitative insights into a comprehensive understanding of prospective student behaviors, motivations, and decision-making. Innovation, Ideation & Experience Planning Lead design thinking workshops, customer journey workshops, ideation sessions, and cross-functional innovation initiatives focused on improving the prospective student experience. Facilitate collaborative discovery sessions with Product, Marketing, Engineering, Analytics, Enrollment, and Content teams to identify customer needs, define opportunities, and align on future-state experiences. Gather, synthesize, and prioritize business, customer, and technical requirements, translating findings into strategic experience recommendations, opportunity assessments, and implementation-ready requirements. Develop future-state journey concepts, service blueprints, experience frameworks, and innovation proposals that improve prospective student engagement and enrollment outcomes. Research emerging trends in customer experience, AI, higher education, and digital innovation to identify new opportunities that strengthen National University's prospective student experience. Influence digital product and experience roadmaps by advocating for prospective student needs, journey improvements, and evidence-based experience decisions. Supervisory Responsi bilities : Individual contributor role that provides leadership through influence and expertise; scope may evolve over time based on organizational needs. Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, Business, Analytics, Statistics, Human-Computer Interaction, or a related field. Master’s degree or M.B.A. preferred. 6 -8 years of experience in UX Strategy, UX Research, Service Design, Customer Experience, or Product Discovery. Experience leading journey mapping, customer research, design thinking workshops, requirements gathering, and cross-functional facilitation. Experience managing research vendors and UX research platforms. Experience designing for higher education, edtech, or other multi-audience environments preferred. Strong portfolio demonstrating user-centered design across complex digital ecosystems. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Deep expertise in qualitative and quantitative research methodologies, customer discovery, experience strategy, and human-centered design principles. Strong experience translating customer insights, behavioral data, and business objectives into strategic recommendations, journey roadmaps, and experience investments. Advanced facilitation, storytelling, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to lead workshops, align diverse perspectives, and build consensus across complex organizations. Expertise in journey mapping, service blueprinting, experience ecosystems, design thinking, and innovation frameworks. Ability to synthesize customer research, market intelligence, competitive analysis, and business priorities into actionable strategies that influence product, marketing, enrollment, and digital experience decisions. Demonstrated ability to influence senior leaders and cross-functional teams through customer insights, strategic thinking, and evidence-based recommendations. Experience developing future-state vision artifacts, experience principles, opportunity frameworks, and strategic roadmaps that guide organizational decision-making. Familiarity with UX research platforms and collaboration tools (User Testing, Userlytics, Dovetail, Miro, Figma, Qualtrics, etc.). Strong understanding of experimentation frameworks, behavioral analytics, conversion optimization, and data-informed experience design practices. Solid understanding of accessibility (WCAG), responsive design principles, content strategy, and digital experience best practices. Exposure to AI, personalization, emerging technologies, and digital innovation trends, with the ability to evaluate their impact on customer experience and business outcomes. Strategic mindset with the ability to balance long-term vision, customer needs, organizational objectives, and execution realities. Exceptional written, verbal, and presentation skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with executives, stakeholders, and cross-functional teams. Ability to work independently, lead through influence, navigate ambiguity, and build strong partnerships across a diverse and matrixed organization. Demonstrated commitment to accountability, continuous improvement, collaboration, and customer-centered decision-making. Location: Remote, USA Travel: up to 10% travel #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Los-Angeles-Center-Los-Angeles-CA/Part-time-Faculty--Applied-Behavioral-Analysis_R20263468-1": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Applied Behavioral Analysis",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $26.63 - $28.89 National University – San Diego, California Part-time Faculty: Applied Behavioral Analysis (Hybrid) Location: Hybrid – Los Angeles National University is a veteran-founded, San Diego-based nonprofit. Since 1971, our mission has been to provide accessible higher education to adult learners. Today, we educate a diverse student body from across the U.S. and around the globe, with more than 230,000 alumni worldwide.  Our three schools and three colleges offer more than 200 accredited and licensed graduate and undergraduate programs. National University holds accreditation through the Western Senior College and Universities Commission (WSCUC). Position Summary The Department of ABA, School Psychology, and Ed Counseling, in the Sanford College of Education at the National University invites applications for part-time faculty in Applied Behavioral Analysis. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of or potential for excellence in teaching in their field and a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. The successful candidate will have the potential for a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. This position primarily works closely with the Academic Program Director and other faculty within the program and contributes to ensuring program quality, student engagement, and success. Essential Job Duties: Provide substantive, timely feedback to students on various assessment activities. Maintain a positive, safe, inclusive student-centric learning environment. Complete required tasks on deadlines (e.g., final grades, assessment, grading rubrics, input for grade appeals, etc.) Maintain appropriate professional training and/or scholarly activities, when applicable. Provide feedback to the course lead regarding the course content. Identify at-risk students and collaborate with student services. Qualifications: Masters ( MA or MS) degree in the field of Applied Behavioral Analysis or related field from a regionally accredited university required. 2 years of higher education teaching experience preferred. Must hold BCBA for a minimum of 5 years and be in good standing with the BACB required. For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following: A cover letter. A curriculum vita. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body. #LI-Hybrid Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
